"sub_response": "George Washington, the first President of the United States, was born on February 22, 1732, in Westmoreland County, Virginia. He was the eldest of six children from his father's second marriage. Washington's father, a farmer and landowner, died when Washington was only 11 years old, leaving him with a modest inheritance. Washington received little formal schooling but had a keen interest in mathematics. At the age of 16, he started working as a surveyor, a profession that provided him with valuable knowledge about the American wilderness. Washington was married to Martha Dandridge Custis, a wealthy widow, in 1759, and the couple had no children together, although Washington raised two children from her previous marriage as his own. Despite his political career, Washington remained closely connected to his family and his Mount Vernon estate, where he enjoyed farming and horse breeding. Washington passed away on December 14, 1799, after serving as the nation's first president."
}

