{"prompt_1": "Please describe the indications and manifestations of heroin dependency in an individual, encompassing alterations in conduct and physical appearance.",
"response_1": "Individuals addicted to heroin may exhibit a variety of signs and symptoms, both in their behavior and physical appearance. Behavioral changes could include erratic mood swings, secretive behavior, decreased motivation, and shifts in sleep patterns. Physical signs may include sudden weight loss, dental problems, scabs or bruises due to skin picking, needle marks, constricted pupils, and a constant runny nose or itching. They may also experience nausea, constipation, difficulty breathing, and withdrawal symptoms such as severe muscle cramps, shaking, and sweating.",
